WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.979
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:08.874
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.174 --> 00:00:15.739
Unit one: Sentences and Punctuation. Today you will write clear sentences with correct punctuation.

4
00:00:16.039 --> 00:00:18.587
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:22.917
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:24.750
Sentence.

7
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.516
Sentence means words that give a complete idea.

8
00:00:29.117 --> 00:00:30.814
Each sentence needs a verb.

9
00:00:31.417 --> 00:00:33.906
Your turn. Say: Sentence.

10
00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:37.965
Sentence.

11
00:00:38.717 --> 00:00:39.822
Capital letter.

12
00:00:40.817 --> 00:00:44.314
Capital letter means a big letter at the start of a sentence.

13
00:00:44.917 --> 00:00:46.533
Begin with a capital letter.

14
00:00:47.117 --> 00:00:50.001
Your turn. Say: Capital letter.

15
00:00:52.867 --> 00:00:53.995
Capital letter.

16
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:55.763
Full stop.

17
00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:59.469
Full stop means the dot at the end of a sentence.

18
00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:01.827
Put a full stop at the end.

19
00:01:02.417 --> 00:01:05.139
Your turn. Say: Full stop.

20
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:08.862
Full stop.

21
00:01:09.617 --> 00:01:10.490
Comma.

22
00:01:11.483 --> 00:01:14.621
Comma means a mark that separates parts of a sentence.

23
00:01:15.217 --> 00:01:16.880
Use a comma in a list.

24
00:01:17.483 --> 00:01:19.660
Your turn. Say: Comma.

25
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.257
Comma.

26
00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.099
Question mark.

27
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:28.547
Question mark means a mark at the end of a question.

28
00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:30.813
Add a question mark here.

29
00:01:31.417 --> 00:01:34.104
Your turn. Say: Question mark.

30
00:01:36.967 --> 00:01:38.293
Question mark.

31
00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:40.109
Subject.

32
00:01:41.117 --> 00:01:43.743
Subject means the person or thing doing the action.

33
00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:46.024
The subject comes first.

34
00:01:46.617 --> 00:01:48.979
Your turn. Say: Subject.

35
00:01:51.833 --> 00:01:52.695
Subject.

36
00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:54.219
Verb.

37
00:01:55.217 --> 00:01:57.762
Verb means a word for an action or state.

38
00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.048
Every sentence has a verb.

39
00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:03.593
Your turn. Say: Verb.

40
00:02:06.433 --> 00:02:07.179
Verb.

41
00:02:07.917 --> 00:02:08.813
Complete.

42
00:02:09.817 --> 00:02:11.723
Complete means with nothing missing.

43
00:02:12.317 --> 00:02:13.910
Write a complete sentence.

44
00:02:14.517 --> 00:02:17.018
Your turn. Say: Complete.

45
00:02:19.867 --> 00:02:20.752
Complete.

46
00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:25.589
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:28.705
Visal, what makes a sentence complete?

48
00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:38.913
A complete sentence has a subject and a verb and gives a full idea. It starts with a capital letter and ends with a full stop.

49
00:02:40.017 --> 00:02:41.378
When do I use a comma?

50
00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:50.441
Use commas to separate items in a list and after words like however. A comma helps the reader pause.

51
00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:53.039
And a question mark?

52
00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:59.751
Use it at the end of a direct question. Never use it after a normal statement.

53
00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:02.911
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.469
Grammar focus: Basic sentence order.

55
00:03:06.769 --> 00:03:08.049
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.622
Sokha writes a short letter.

57
00:03:11.517 --> 00:03:14.306
The students read books, magazines and news.

58
00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:21.098
Start with a capital letter, include a subject and a verb, and end with a full stop or a question mark.

59
00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:25.361
Be careful! Don't say: sokha write a letter

60
00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.543
Say: Sokha writes a letter.

61
00:03:29.843 --> 00:03:31.750
Capital letter and verb s.

62
00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:35.196
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.326
A Clear Message.

64
00:03:37.626 --> 00:03:40.009
Sokha writes a message to his teacher.

65
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.580
He begins every sentence with a capital letter.

66
00:03:44.567 --> 00:03:47.193
He puts commas between the items in his list.

67
00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.664
He ends each sentence with a full stop.

68
00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:53.898
Then he checks the punctuation again.

69
00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.897
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.017
A sentence begins with a blank letter.

71
00:04:02.317 --> 00:04:05.424
A, blue. B, capital. C, small.

72
00:04:08.967 --> 00:04:11.024
The answer is B: capital.

73
00:04:12.183 --> 00:04:14.009
A full stop ends a blank.

74
00:04:14.309 --> 00:04:17.753
A, word. B, page. C, sentence.

75
00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.381
The answer is C: sentence.

76
00:04:24.517 --> 00:04:26.121
Use a comma in a blank.

77
00:04:26.421 --> 00:04:29.715
A, list. B, name. C, number.

78
00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:34.988
The answer is A: list.

79
00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:38.208
A question needs a question blank.

80
00:04:38.508 --> 00:04:41.522
A, line. B, mark. C, word.

81
00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:46.927
The answer is B: mark.

82
00:04:48.083 --> 00:04:50.071
Sokha checks his blank again.

83
00:04:50.371 --> 00:04:54.164
A, bicycle. B, lunch. C, punctuation.

84
00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:00.164
The answer is C: punctuation.

85
00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:04.600
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:07.078
How do you write a clear sentence?

87
00:05:15.883 --> 00:05:17.395
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:17.695 --> 00:05:29.394
I start with a capital letter and include a subject and a verb. I use commas in lists and end with a full stop or a question mark. Then I check the punctuation.

89
00:05:29.694 --> 00:05:31.624
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:32.517 --> 00:05:36.655
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and basic sentence order.

91
00:05:36.955 --> 00:05:40.908
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

92
00:05:41.208 --> 00:05:43.547
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

93
00:05:43.847 --> 00:05:46.905
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

